/** @mainpage Qore VSS Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section vssintro Introduction to the VSS Module

    The %VssLoader module provides support for the
    <a href="https://covesa.github.io/vehicle_signal_specification/">COVESA Vehicle Signal Specification (VSS)</a>,
    the industry-standard data model for vehicle signals.

    This module is released under the MIT license (see <a href="COPYING.MIT">COPYING.MIT</a>
    for details).

    To use this module, use \c "%requires VssLoader" in your code.

    All the public symbols in the module are defined in the VssLoader namespace.

    @section vssmodules User Modules

    The following user modules are provided with this module:
    - @ref vssloaderintro "VssLoader": Core VSS loading, parsing, and validation functionality
    - <img src="vss-logo.svg" width="28" height="28" alt="VssDataProvider app icon"/> @ref vssdataproviderintro "VssDataProvider": DataProvider integration for browsable VSS catalog and pipeline data processors for telemetry normalization, validation, unit conversion, and enrichment

    @section vsscapabilities Capabilities

    - Native \c .vspec file parsing with \#include directive resolution
    - Instance expansion (e.g. \c "Row[1,4]" to concrete paths)
    - Overlay merging (attribute override, path addition/deletion)
    - Pre-exported VSS JSON/YAML loading
    - Data validation against VSS catalogs (type, range, enum checks)
    - Extensible unit conversion (factor/offset model)
    - DataProvider browsable tree navigation
    - Pipeline processors: normalize, validate, convert, enrich

    @section vssexamples Examples

    @subpage vssexamplesguide


    @section vssreleasenotes Release Notes

